{"baseRefName":"main","body":"The kinetic-response test previously required registered hidden scalar/velocity fields. This change derives a necessary residual directly in calibrated lensing and actual-event redshift primitives, with every record derivative transferred to candidate/test weights. It eliminates the explicit hidden-field and density-initial-value inputs for this test; it does not derive the action class, background, calibration or temporal coverage.\n\nThe self-contained note composes the kinetic equation, momentum/Euler elimination and ordered photon adjoints. An explicit noncanonical original-action solution gives zero for its own kinetic coefficient and the exact nonzero moment `827093/50599790841600` for the fixed U=0 alternative on the same background. Exact rational Bernstein enclosures supply a deterministic harmonic-coefficient error budget. The sufficient radius is about 1.02718e-8 at unit mode normalization, scales with perturbation amplitude and is not an instrumental precision claim. No empirical data or independent experimental holdout is used.\n\nValidation includes original-action 82/0, primitive 78/0 and bound 42/0 controls (overlapping families), independent adjoint, original-action photon-path, norm and temporal-access derivations, and bounded final source/output comparison. The five-source isolated replay matches the canonical result byte for byte. All three helpers are imported by the primary; the bound consumes freshly computed kernels in memory. Fresh cache, vocabulary, syntax, links, exact source bindings and staged diff checks pass. The citation manifest adds only this note node on base 6ee7a70e.\n\nActual-source mutations cover spatial sign, spherical divergence/Laplacian, latent sign, redshift-path factor, radial ordering, time measure, product rules, and Bernstein conversion/area/upper bound. Eleven full mutated runs produce explicit false controls. Two full runs time out; targeted execution of their unchanged affected definitions detects the two omitted terms with baseline positive controls. Those narrower checks are not called completed full reruns. Three previously completed action-family mutations apply to the byte-identical action helper now on main, with exact evidence bindings.\n\nPreserved failures include an initial ray window crossing the background singularity, an undetected spatial sign under the original harmonic-only fixture, two norm-checker mistakes, two full mutation timeouts, a tuple/JSON comparison mismatch, and mechanical packaging failures. The accepted full-ray window was fixed before recomputation. The note distinguishes normalized harmonic-coefficient errors from arbitrary sky-pixel errors and states the missing reception-time, background, gain, angular-extraction and nonlinear-error suppliers. No unique action, full-equation sufficiency, initial-state origin, absolute scale or TOE claim is made.\n\nClaim type: bounded_theorem. Current surface: conditional-support / upstream_support. One coherent milestone is supported by the focused independent value proposal. Full pipeline, strict audit lint, changed-audit-evidence and any formal audit remain the shared exact integrated-main landing gate. No audit verdict, main push or merge is performed by this change.\n\nReview and reproducibility entry points: `docs/SCALAR_PRIMITIVE_KINETIC_NOTE_2026-10-16.md`, `scripts/scalar_primitive_kinetic.py`, and `.claude/science/physics-loops/scalar-primitive-kinetic-20261016/EVIDENCE_INDEX.md`. The evidence archive and final supplement preserve source/code, exposure boundaries, real failures and exact member hashes. Root personally authored the research; subagents supplied focused checks. Scheduling was deleted at the user's request.\n\nMain advanced to de540f645a after branch preparation. Object-only conflict inspection finds only `docs/audit/data/citation_graph_manifest.json`; no science or workflow file conflicts. Regenerate that manifest from the exact integrated tree in the shared landing lane. This is a pending landing condition, not a source-math failure.\n","files":[{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/scalar-primitive-kinetic-20261016/APPROACH_REGISTRY.md","additions":12,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/scalar-primitive-kinetic-20261016/ARTIFACT_PLAN.md","additions":7,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/scalar-primitive-kinetic-20261016/ASSUMPTIONS_AND_IMPORTS.md","additions":7,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/scalar-primitive-kinetic-20261016/BASE_REFRESH_v1.json","additions":17,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/scalar-primitive-kinetic-20261016/CACHE_RECEIPT_v1.json","additions":17,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/scalar-primitive-kinetic-20261016/CACHE_RECEIPT_v2.json","additions":18,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/scalar-primitive-kinetic-20261016/CANONICALIZATION_v1.json","additions":15,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/scalar-primitive-kinetic-20261016/CANONICAL_CORRESPONDENCE_v1.json","additions":11,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/scalar-primitive-kinetic-20261016/CANONICAL_PROOF_FREEZE_v1.json","additions":12,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/scalar-primitive-kinetic-20261016/CANONICAL_RUN_v1.json","additions":30,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/scalar-primitive-kinetic-20261016/CANONICAL_RUN_v1.stderr","additions":0,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/scalar-primitive-kinetic-20261016/CANONICAL_RUN_v1.stdout","additions":203,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/scalar-primitive-kinetic-20261016/CANONICAL_SOURCE_FREEZE_v1.json","additions":11,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/scalar-primitive-kinetic-20261016/CANONICAL_SOURCE_FREEZE_v2.json","additions":11,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/scalar-primitive-kinetic-20261016/CITATION_GRAPH_RECEIPT_v1.j